# promise: #876
# An inactive window on macOS Dark lays a one-colour space and a dark gradient on Arc's dark grey (25 and 27.5),
# so the sidebar goes darker when the window loses focus, as Arc's does (Arc 1.174.3, 27 Nov 2026). Cra laid them on
# 212 and went lighter. On macOS Light the grey stays Arc's 212. deactivate=<label> makes Cra inactive without bringing
# another app forward; systemAppearance flips the app's appearance, which Cra reads as macOS's here.
# Active on macOS Dark, the one-colour space blurs through a darker material, 35 + 0.35 · backdrop (35 over black,
# 124 over white), as Arc 1.174 does (28 Nov 2026); Cra used macOS Light's 66 / 198, lighter and
# more see-through than Arc's (#876, "even with the slider all the way up it still appears semi-translucent").
budget rss=600 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
